// Hunt: ClickFix split-flag string concatenation
// Table: DeviceCustomScriptEvents
// Source: pattern confirmed against a real in-the-wild ClickFix command
//         that used ('-Windo' + 'wStyle') ('hid' + 'den') to split
//         -WindowStyle and hidden into two quoted fragments joined with +.
//         The existing heavy concatenation hunt (ConcatHits >= 8) missed
//         this sample entirely, it only has two + operators total, well
//         under that threshold.
// Purpose: catches the specific micro-pattern of a single quoted fragment,
//          plus operator, second quoted fragment, inside parentheses,
//          regardless of how many times it repeats in the surrounding
//          script or command line. This is a lower threshold, more
//          targeted companion to the ConcatHits >= 8 heuristic, aimed at
//          exactly this kind of flag or cmdlet name fragmentation used to
//          dodge literal keyword matching.
// Validated: success. Regex confirmed via print against the literal
//          fragment ('-Windo' + 'wStyle') shown above, and returns 0 rows
//          when no split-flag pattern is present, a clean result.
// Quick summary: Flags a flag or cmdlet name split into two quoted fragments
// joined with +, catching obfuscation the high-threshold concat hunt misses.
DeviceCustomScriptEvents
| where Timestamp > ago(7d)
| where isnotempty(ScriptContent) or isnotempty(InitiatingProcessCommandLine)
| where (ScriptContent matches regex @'\(\s*''[\-A-Za-z]{2,}''\s*\+\s*''[\-A-Za-z]{2,}''\s*\)'
        or ScriptContent matches regex @'\(\s*"[\-A-Za-z]{2,}"\s*\+\s*"[\-A-Za-z]{2,}"\s*\)')
    or (InitiatingProcessCommandLine matches regex @'\(\s*''[\-A-Za-z]{2,}''\s*\+\s*''[\-A-Za-z]{2,}''\s*\)'
        or InitiatingProcessCommandLine matches regex @'\(\s*"[\-A-Za-z]{2,}"\s*\+\s*"[\-A-Za-z]{2,}"\s*\)')
| project Timestamp, DeviceName, InitiatingProcessAccountName, InitiatingProcessFileName, InitiatingProcessCommandLine, ScriptContent, RuleName
| order by Timestamp desc
| take 10000
